
              DayDream BBS V1.00, ConversionTableXX.DAT
              -----------------------------------------

ConversionTableXX.DAT-files are 256 bytes long and therefore contain a
slot  (unsigned byte) for  each character  in an 8-BIT ASCII table. XX
should be replaced with a two digit decimal value from 01 to 99. These
files  are used  during a remote-session  for character  conversion in
order to  make special  characters, such  as  scandinavian  alphabets,
appear correctly  in both, the  remote and local  screens. In the data
file, DayDream:Data/Display.DAT, you  can separately  for each display
mode specify  which conversion table to use for  incoming and outgoing
characters.  After configuring  this option, you'll  never  hear  your
users complaining that they don't see all  the characters  as supposed
to. Characters must appear in the same order as in 8-BIT ASCII table!!
